This post exists only to exercise the article layout while the website is being
built. It must not appear in a production build, the RSS feed, or the sitemap.

## A representative section

Real posts will be a place to explore ideas honestly: what seems interesting,
where it connects to existing work, and what remains uncertain. The design
should make ordinary prose comfortable to read without making every paragraph
feel like a manifesto.

> A block quote is included here so its spacing, color, and typography can be
> designed before a real article depends on them.

The final article system should also handle [references](https://example.com),
inline `code`, lists, figures, and richer Svelte components when they are
actually useful.

- A short list item
- Another item with enough text to wrap on a narrow screen
- A final item for checking vertical rhythm
